-- examples/checks/asks-reads-everything.rofl — A RULE IN THE CONE SEES EVERY RELATION'S ROWS.
-- au_any is asked and reads derived_by with its fact unbound: the rows of every relation's firings are
-- its premise, so the cone is the whole world and au_b is derived although nothing names it. The kernel's
-- cells, members, lattice members and dominations are read the same way (asks-reads-cells.rofl).
asks(au_any).
edb(au_src).
au_src(1). au_src(2).
au_a(X) :- au_src(X).
au_b(X) :- au_src(X).
au_any(R) :- derived_by[$kernel](_, R, _).
-- expect-row: au_a[main](1)
-- expect-row: au_b[main](1)
